    "publication_date": "2026-07-10",
    "description": "<p>This record is the current public workflow and replication packet for the Modern LaTeX Manuscripts project. It describes the actual AI-run process: source intake, source-identity and page-map checks, local GPU OCR/VLM witness generation, page-unit TeX reconstruction, mathematical translation, local-to-web review handoffs, deterministic repair, compile/render gates, conservative status labels, GitHub maintenance, and reader-first Zenodo publication.</p><p><strong>Read first:</strong> <code>00_AI_Run_Modern_LaTeX_Manuscript_Workflow_Current_20260710.pdf</code>. The Markdown source and grouped ZIP contain supporting workflow documents and the July SGA6 source-rescribe method lesson.</p><p><strong>New in this version:</strong> a concrete failure catalogue from the SGA6 source-rescribe. A compile-clean scaffold contained whole-page compression, omitted proofs, an invented lemma statement, a wrong identity value, altered notation, and unsupported equation tags. A nearby tag was genuine, so mathematical objects and tags must be verified individually against source witnesses rather than repaired by pattern.</p><p><strong>Status rule:</strong> this workflow record is not a critical edition and does not certify any author corpus. OCR, VLM, formula crops, generated TeX, agent outputs, and compile logs remain witness or workpass layers unless a source-specific audit promotes a declared locus.</p><p><strong>GitHub:</strong> workflow corrections and reproducibility improvements can be suggested through issues or pull requests at <a href=\"https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts\">https://github.com/KokunoYumeto/modern-latex-manuscripts</a>.</p>",
